  "note": "Spain issues a single HAREC-based amateur authorisation (the harmonised exam certificate under CEPT T/R 61-02); there are no operator sub-categories with different frequency access, so privileges are uniform. The frequency table is the CNAF; the cw/data/phone/image mode segmentation is the IARU Region 1 band plan used as the working table (the Spanish regulation itself defers to the IARU R1 band plan as general practice). Power limits (Orden IET/1311/2013 annex 3.1): 1000 W PEP on 160-10m, 600 W PEP on 6m/4m/2m, 300 W PEP on 70cm, 1000 W e.i.r.p. from 23cm up; emissions in secondary-status bands are limited to 50% of those values; 1 W e.i.r.p. on 2200m and 630m (up to 5 W e.i.r.p. on 630m more than 800 km from African borders). EME/meteor-scatter stations may run up to 1000 W PEP in the IARU-recommended sub-bands outside urban areas. Unattended stations: max 50 W on HF and 50 W on VHF/UHF outside urban areas (10 W inside). No 60m allocation. Special authorisations from the Secretaría de Estado are required for temporary/experimental uses outside the CNAF (e.g. the historic 40.65-40.75 MHz experimental grant).",
